## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design cross-region consistency with SLA targets and fault tolerance for multi-tenant streams.

## Key Concepts
- Total order per tenant across regions
- Vector clocks and regional sequence numbers
- Barrier commits, idempotent processing, and tombstones
- Fault injection and late-arrival handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Vector clock merge for per-tenant streams
function mergeVC(a, b) {
  const keys = new Set([...Object.keys(a), ...Object.keys(b)]);
  const out = {};
  for (const k of keys) {
    out[k] = Math.max(a[k] || 0, b[k] || 0);
  }
  return out;
}

// Regional sequencer generates monotonically increasing sequence
class RegionalSequencer {
  constructor(region) {
    this.region = region;
    this.sequences = new Map(); // tenantId -> sequence number
  }

  next(tenantId) {
    const current = this.sequences.get(tenantId) || 0;
    const next = current + 1;
    this.sequences.set(tenantId, next);
    return { tenantId, sequence: next, region: this.region };
  }
}
```

Why This Is Asked
- Validates per-tenant auditable trails without impacting throughput
- Ensures tamper evidence via signatures and secure storage
- Checks ability to query across tenants with predictable retention

Key Concepts
- Append-only logs, tenant isolation, data integrity, retention strategy
- Tamper detection using MACs or signatures, and secure storage backends
- API design for write/read with minimal surface area and clear semantics

Code Example
```javascript
class AuditLog {
  constructor(storage, signer) {
    this.storage = storage; // per-tenant append-only store
    this.signer = signer;   // cryptographic signing service
  }

  async write(tenant, event) {
    const entry = {
      timestamp: Date.now(),
      tenant,
      event,
      signature: await this.signer.sign(event)
    };
    return await this.storage.append(tenant, entry);
  }

  async query(tenant, since, limit) {
    const entries = await this.storage.read(tenant, since, limit);
    return entries.filter(entry => 
      this.signer.verify(entry.event, entry.signature)
    );
  }
}
```

